{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals","id":1177932,"title":"\"Powerful\" mortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-21T13:43:43-08:00","id":1177932,"title":"\"Powerful\" mortals","content":"How could I give some powers to mortals? I'm thinking to a &quot;The Hunters Hunted&quot;-ish approach, in which the characters are completely mortals, but have some limited supernatural powers, like hedge magic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My English sucks. Sorry.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23549-toreadorgentleman","name":"ToreadorGentleman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T13:46:04-08:00","id":1177933,"title":"","content":"Short answer:<br /> First edition: World of Darkness: Second Sight or Hunter: the Vigil.<br /> Second edition: Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook or The God-Machine Rules Update's Supernatural Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-21T15:05:06-08:00","id":1177948,"title":"","content":"Or Hunter, some Conspiracies have supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T19:50:12-08:00","id":1179064,"title":"","content":"Gutter magic in hunter<br /> <br /> Ghouls are still mortals and need to feed their addiction<br /> <br /> wolf-blooded could be a good choice<br /> <br /> Lucifuge with the hellfire castigation can scare vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-24T21:55:43-08:00","id":1179108,"title":"","content":"Mechanically you could just give them Dread Powers representing whatever supernatural ability you want them to have.<br /> <br /> Give an NPC Prodigious Leap, Snare, and Wall Climb and you have Spider-man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T07:50:32-08:00","id":1179195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179064#post1179064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gutter magic in hunter<br /> <br /> Ghouls are still mortals and need to feed their addiction<br /> <br /> wolf-blooded could be a good choice<br /> <br /> Lucifuge with the hellfire castigation can scare vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>I know Cruac requires Vitae, but is there any reason a mortal can't use Theban Sorcery (other than that it is categorized as a Discipline)? Or something similar, mechanically (so as to prevent drawing from non-Vampire books, since this is in the Vampire sub-forum)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:25:06-08:00","id":1179249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179195#post1179195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know Cruac requires Vitae, but is there any reason a mortal can't use Theban Sorcery (other than that it is categorized as a Discipline)? Or something similar, mechanically (so as to prevent drawing from non-Vampire books, since this is in the Vampire sub-forum)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, Theban Sorcery is pretty much in the hands of the Lancea et Sanctum, so that's one reason. Otherwise, it is a discipline, so only vampire related beings can use it.<br /> <br /> However, at least in 2e, it does mention that Theban Sorcery might have been a mortal sorcery that the Kindred adapted to themselves. So a group of mortals that use said precursor sorcery isn't out of the question. I would just have it tied behind some sort of mystery cult for added depth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T10:57:37-08:00","id":1179257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179249#post1179249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, Theban Sorcery is pretty much in the hands of the Lancea et Sanctum, so that's one reason. Otherwise, it is a discipline, so only vampire related beings can use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's why I covered that. It is represented as a Discipline, but it doesn't really seem to <i>fit</i> what Disciplines are, and most Miracles don't require anything a mortal couldn't provide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179249#post1179249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, at least in 2e, it does mention that Theban Sorcery might have been a mortal sorcery that the Kindred adapted to themselves. So a group of mortals that use said precursor sorcery isn't out of the question. I would just have it tied behind some sort of mystery cult for added depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. I was mostly saying &quot;use Theban as a mechanical example&quot; so the OP wouldn't have to reference non-Vampire books. Mortals could use their I-can't-believe-it's-not-Theban magic that just happens to also use extended rolls, sacrifices, and Willpower to achieve supernatural effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-25T19:42:28-08:00","id":1179405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179108#post1179108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechanically you could just give them Dread Powers representing whatever supernatural ability you want them to have.<br /> <br /> Give an NPC Prodigious Leap, Snare, and Wall Climb and you have Spider-man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Needs increased strength and stamina; not sure if Spider-man was within the five dot max, or not, but he was certainly strong and tough. Also, something to sense danger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T07:45:34-08:00","id":1179513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179405#post1179405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Needs increased strength and stamina; not sure if Spider-man was within the five dot max, or not, but he was certainly strong and tough. Also, something to sense danger. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>While his strength and stamina aren't particularly notable compared to Marvel's true heavy hitters like Thor, Hulk, Sentry etc., he's still way above the fifth dot in either Attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:16:06-08:00","id":1179533,"title":"","content":"Absolutely but that's easy to factor in (and Horrors aren't limited to the 1-5 spread normal humans are). Powerful mortals are all over in Chronicles of Darkness and they're easy to represent without needing to delve into other gamelines, though you can do that as well.<br /> <br /> The Chronicles of Darkness book has rules for making 'standard' antagonists, ephemerals, and horrors (like Spider-man would be, in the Chronicles of Darkness, if designed as an antagonist).<br /> <br /> Otherwise, if you do have access to a wide variety of books a number have been mentioned above you can source for powers, abilities and oddities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-26-2018, 01:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T10:21:26-08:00","id":1179535,"title":"","content":"Well... spiderman is able to lift 10 tons so that is the equivalent of a strength 29 being according to the WoD strenght table XD. (Well lets say a little less than 29 since there is a roll to do to increase the feats of strength achivable, but still we are far more above the maximum reacheable by a bp 5 Vampire with vigor and Strength at max (without considering frenzy and vitae spent to increase attributes).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-26T11:50:59-08:00","id":1179561,"title":"","content":"There are some antagonists in thousand years of night that count as powerful mortals as well. There was that Deborah, who was a mostly mortal person with some biblical magic at her command. Then there were also the Sons of Phobos, blood sorcerers that have a penchant for devouring hearts for power, with ghoul and kindred hearts being really potent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T16:51:15-08:00","id":1180285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179535#post1179535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... spiderman is able to lift 10 tons so that is the equivalent of a strength 29 being according to the WoD strenght table XD. (Well lets say a little less than 29 since there is a roll to do to increase the feats of strength achivable, but still we are far more above the maximum reacheable by a bp 5 Vampire with vigor and Strength at max (without considering frenzy and vitae spent to increase attributes).</div> </div> </div> </div>10 tons? Why? How does he not maim criminals by accident?<br /> <br /> Does every superhero have a 'cardboard world' speech ready to go?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T17:18:55-08:00","id":1180292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1180285#post1180285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">10 tons? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Proportional strength of a spider, of course. Nature's second strongest arachnid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does he not maim criminals by accident? </div> </div> </div>I think he has to really push for that, but he's usually called out as one of the potentially greatest of superheroes in Marvel, across all stats, he just doesn't get to that point because he's supposed to be eternally stuck in not-quite-being-an-adult, psychologically.<br /> <br /> But really I was just trying to show how you could use Dread Powers to imitate things 'powerful' mortals might have, and in depth discussions about Spider-man have probably been tackled better elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-28T19:28:58-08:00","id":1180324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1180285#post1180285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 10 tons? Why? How does he not maim criminals by accident?<br /> <br /> Does every superhero have a 'cardboard world' speech ready to go?</div> </div> </div> </div>A combination of things really. One, most of the villains he fights have equipment and/or powers to compensate for his strength or cancel or weaken his powers. (Sandman, Venom, Jackal, Rhino, Dr. Octopus) Two, as nofather mentioned, he consciously pulls his punches most of the time especially if he 'knows' he's dealing with a normal person. Three, he usually makes a point of trying to avoid direct physical contact, often using his uncanny agility to avoid getting hit to wear down his opponents and equipment to slow down or stop criminals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 01-29-2018, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T11:10:04-08:00","id":1180457,"title":"","content":"Oh, another thing you might be able to do is use the mechanics of some of the Disciplines (probably the physical ones, mostly) as &quot;cybernetic augmentation&quot;. Vigor seems like it can model mechanical limb super strength just as easily as magical undead super strength. Similar for Celerity and Resilience. The more &quot;mystic&quot; Disciplines are harder to justify, but might be possible via either pseudo-science or psychic powers.<br /> <br /> It does depend on how you want to take the Chronicle's themes and mood, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T20:47:29-08:00","id":1180594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1180292#post1180292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Proportional strength of a spider, of course. Nature's second strongest arachnid.</div> </div> </div> </div>1.) I wasn't really looking for an answer. That was more exasperation than actual questioning. I seem to have an innate dislike of the ... word... eh... mythic? I like when characters have an advantage or two they use well, instead of being unrivaled. As my conception of Spiderman was 'stronger than he looks' and then Marcus goes and informs me that he can lift cars... It just annoyed me somehow.<br /> <br /> 2.) Second strongest? What's the strongest? (actual questions this time. :P )<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1180292#post1180292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> in depth discussions about Spider-man have probably been tackled better elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Cheers for weighting in regardless; don't take the above as me giving out TO YOU. I'm just giving out in general. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-29T21:01:58-08:00","id":1180596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tabanese</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1180594#post1180594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.) I wasn't really looking for an answer. That was more exasperation than actual questioning. I seem to have an innate dislike of the ... word... eh... mythic? I like when characters have an advantage or two they use well, instead of being unrivaled. As my conception of Spiderman was 'stronger than he looks' and then Marcus goes and informs me that he can lift cars... It just annoyed me somehow.<br /> <br /> 2.) Second strongest? What's the strongest? (actual questions this time. :P )</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an attempt at a joke. The in-world reason for his power is him getting the proportionate strength of a spider, but as far as I know spiders aren't exactly known for being strong, so I don't get it myself, though I know of it. And I admit this is just guesswork, but I figure a scorpion would be physically stronger, if only because they're more made for grabbing things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-01T17:17:57-08:00","id":1181528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1180596#post1180596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was an attempt at a joke. The in-world reason for his power is him getting the proportionate strength of a spider, but as far as I know spiders aren't exactly known for being strong, so I don't get it myself, though I know of it. And I admit this is just guesswork, but I figure a scorpion would be physically stronger, if only because they're more made for grabbing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>And scorpions are arachnids? Huh, TIL. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T07:46:31-08:00","id":1181658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1180596#post1180596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was an attempt at a joke. The in-world reason for his power is him getting the proportionate strength of a spider, but as far as I know spiders aren't exactly known for being strong, so I don't get it myself, though I know of it. And I admit this is just guesswork, but I figure a scorpion would be physically stronger, if only because they're more made for grabbing things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiders, like most arthropods, can lift objects weighing several times their own body mass. This has little to do with them being particularly strong and everything to do with the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square%E2%80%93cube_law\" target=\"_blank\">square-cube law</a> and how it interacts with living beings - simply put, the smaller the creature, the smaller percentage of its muscle power is used to lift the weight of the body, leaving more &quot;excess strength&quot; to be applied externally.<br /> <br /> Now, if you forget the laws of the universe that make this possible, if a human-sized being could lift as much in relation to their body mass as a spider could, this would be a pretty impressive (and clearly superhuman) show of strength.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-02T18:46:01-08:00","id":1181883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1181658#post1181658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The smaller the creature, the smaller percentage of its muscle power is used to lift the weight of the body, leaving more &quot;excess strength&quot; to be applied externally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I am such a great lover. #powerfulmortal #stillontopic :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-05T07:39:58-08:00","id":1182595,"title":"","content":"Hurt Locker has a bunch of minor templates, some of which can get strong enough to pose a threat to vampires<br /> <br /> And of course anybody with the psychokinesis (specifically pyro variant) merit can do a lot of damage very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-06T08:39:36-08:00","id":1182940,"title":"","content":"Best answer is probably going to remain:<br /> 1. If mortals are PCs, use supernatural merits and McGuffin a way to acquire more during play.<br /> 2. If mortals are NPCs, use horrors rules to build them, throw in supernatural merits if you want, and go to town.<br /> <br /> You could combine these, and let PCs use horror rules to build characters, but it seems like a lot of work for something you could just as easily handwave into &quot;new&quot; supernatural merits if you want.<br /> <br /> The main CofD forum page here has some additional ideas scattered through it for homebrew supernatural merits that are not splat-related. <br /> <br /> You can also stack minor splats to gain an approximation of the desired effect, if the characters are intended to be mixed up with specific supernatural types.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf<br /> <br /> PS. Full disclosure: my preferred play is &quot;powerful mortal&quot; range for my own PCs, regardless of splat chosen and group makeup. Someone has to be justifiably paranoid!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T13:49:05-08:00","id":1183371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1179257#post1179257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, that's why I covered that. It is represented as a Discipline, but it doesn't really seem to <i>fit</i> what Disciplines are, and most Miracles don't require anything a mortal couldn't provide.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right. I was mostly saying &quot;use Theban as a mechanical example&quot; so the OP wouldn't have to reference non-Vampire books. Mortals could use their I-can't-believe-it's-not-Theban magic that just happens to also use extended rolls, sacrifices, and Willpower to achieve supernatural effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did that for years without ever giving a damn. Hell, my &quot;lycanthropes&quot; were just rogue ghoul families with Protean in their package. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T15:17:15-08:00","id":1183404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1183371#post1183371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Did that for years without ever giving a damn. Hell, my &amp;quot;lycanthropes&amp;quot; were just rogue ghoul families with Protean in their package. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Got their Vitae via a lot of &quot;red meat&quot;, eh?<br /> <br /> It isn't a bad way to run things, if you want the themes/flavor of other Splats/monsters without having to rifle through a bunch of books.<br /> <br /> Mages: various &quot;mental&quot; Disciplines and some !Blood Magic?<br /> How about other monsters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:18:02-08:00","id":1183434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1183404#post1183404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Got their Vitae via a lot of &quot;red meat&quot;, eh?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually from hunting kindred, sometimes capturing neonates, chaining them to cellars where they were periodically thrown &quot;live food&quot; and then ritually exsanguinated them, among other stuff. The fact the various &quot;weres&quot; while still mostly divided by family/animal would have not much qualms about making occassional deals or mixing up added even more confusion to my players, who were used to Werewolf and had no idea from what context i was working from (some native american folklore from Brazil mixed in with obscure regional traditions). Horrid fun times. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1183404#post1183404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't a bad way to run things, if you want the themes/flavor of other Splats/monsters without having to rifle through a bunch of books.<br /> <br /> Mages: various &quot;mental&quot; Disciplines and some !Blood Magic?<br /> How about other monsters?</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, i wasn't even caring for the themes/flavor of other splats. Keeping things to Requiem made quite clear to everybody they should not take anything from the books for granted as canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T17:49:34-08:00","id":1183445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1183434#post1183434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually from hunting kindred, sometimes capturing neonates, chaining them to cellars where they were periodically thrown &quot;live food&quot; and then ritually exsanguinated them, among other stuff. The fact the various &quot;weres&quot; while still mostly divided by family/animal would have not much qualms about making occassional deals or mixing up added even more confusion to my players, who were used to Werewolf and had no idea from what context i was working from (some native american folklore from Brazil mixed in with obscure regional traditions). Horrid fun times. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>So pure Ghoul, then? Not werewolf-modelled-as-a-Ghoul-Family?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1183434#post1183434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Truth be told, i wasn't even caring for the themes/flavor of other splats. Keeping things to Requiem made quite clear to everybody they should not take anything from the books for granted as canon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more the general themes of the archetypes - witch, fae creature, reanimated person, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-07T18:47:08-08:00","id":1183458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1183445#post1183445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So pure Ghoul, then? Not werewolf-modelled-as-a-Ghoul-Family?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very successful branch of &quot;masterless&quot; Ghoul families with a peculiar mythology mixed in that justified their kindred-hunting in more ways than one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1183445#post1183445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant more the general themes of the archetypes - witch, fae creature, reanimated person, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, yes, more of that indeed, with some funky brewing along the way, like mages &amp; witches as separate &quot;lesser templates&quot;, mummies (far from canon back then), ghost-blooded (ghost-dhampirs so to speak), sirens and other interesting beings.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-12T08:58:38-08:00","id":1185210,"title":"","content":"In my opinion any Hunter game is always about a group of people coming from all fringes of society to fight monsters they know so little of, normal people, with unique (non-supernatural) abilities and limited resources.<br /> <br /> They know their weaknesses and know that a direct confrontation will most likely end in their certain death, so they learned to use other assets to strike at the supernatural influences. Cunning ways and group formation is key.<br /> <br /> But if you insist, there's a number of Supernatural merits in Chronicles of Darkness Corebook to give your Hunter an edge, I also think Hunter: The Vigil offer Hunters some supernatural advantages (though I never used Hunter: The Vigil to run Hunter games myself)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-13T20:16:17-08:00","id":1185814,"title":"","content":"I have a collection of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801745#post801745\">24 Minor Templates</a> which essentially makes someone equal supernatural footing as a Potency 1 Horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-14T05:43:25-08:00","id":1185908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1177932-powerful-mortals?p=1185814#post1185814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a collection of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader?p=801745#post801745\">24 Minor Templates</a> which essentially makes someone equal supernatural footing as a Potency 1 Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. I like how they basically (with minor variation) use the Horror rules to create some minor human character types. A bit verbose, if not using your full expanded rule set, but I can see how they were designed to fit into a common system. Ever thought about scaling them back into CofD Core and posting them (well, characters that are examples of them) in the The Horror Show (like your simplified monsters)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}